// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row match_array_nested_array_subpattern_mlirgen_malfunction (tier 3, refuses). AN
// ARRAY PATTERN NESTED INSIDE AN ARRAY PATTERN BINDS NOTHING AND MLIR-GEN SELF-DIAGNOSES.
//
// `match arr { [[x, _]] => x.v }` over `[[D; 2]; 1]`: rustc 1.98.1 compiles and runs it, k=1 n=12,
// exit 0 (twin src/compiler/probes/2026-09-16j-arrpath2/ybat/rust/y05.rs, MEASURED). TODAY logosc
// exits 1 with NO `error:` diagnostic at all — it self-diagnoses in the backend:
//     mlir_gen: warning: undefined 'x' in fn 'hb_y05$g__f__pmut_i64' — no value emitted
//     mlir_gen: internal: `let __ret_tmp_0` initializer produced no value (expr kind 14) — DROPPED
//     mlir_gen: internal: `return` value lowered to no value (expr kind 4) — the RETURN was silently
